  "worked_solution": "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e82+t,1+3t,2t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ \u27e8x,y,z\u27e9\\cdot \u27e83,-2,4\u27e9 & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot \u27e83,-2,4\u27e9 & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e82+t,1+3t,2t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e83,-2,4\u27e9 & =-6 \\\\ \u27e82+t,1+3t,2t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e83,-2,4\u27e9 & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e82+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e80,-5,-4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$",
